  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 107 AM MDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nWhile the new upper low center remains across far south central or\nsoutheast NM on Friday night, an upper level high will be building\nin from the northwest. The upper high will become more and more\ndominant over NM through the weekend allowing temperatures to\nclimb, and keeping precipitation chances nil. Light winds are \nexpected Saturday, but easterly flow increases a bit on Sunday. A \nfew gusts near 20-25 mph will develop during the afternoon. \nOtherwise, it should be a beautiful weekend to get outside.\n\nNot much change is in store for Monday as the upper high weakens.\nIt continues to look like an upper level shortwave will cross NM\non Tuesday. Models are struggling with the details, but it does\nlook like at least some precipitation will be in store. The GFS\nand GEFS are more robust with precipitation than other models \nthough. Some light precipitation may linger Wednesday, but another\nupper high should begin building over the Desert Southwest.",
